I would just about always take a mithril coat over a well-enchanted
bit of heavy armor if using the latter meant being encumbered;
especially if I lack speed. (Fairly) lightweight, immune to rust/
corrosion, great stuff. I can't stand being encumbered, and one of my
more successful strategies has always been "Run away! Run away!"
Creating stashes can be tedious but necessary... although if you have
a ton of food, this is the least annoying stuff to stash, and I
sometimes don't bother dragging it along to a proper stash, but simply
drop it near a stairwell for easy access. Also, if deciding which food
to carry, consider the different food items' nutrition to weight
ratios: lembas being the big winner of course, and pancakes, eggs, and
royal jelly are most worthy; while C-rations, the majority of fruit
(not slime molds!) and the delicious but very insubstantial cream pie
are the worst offenders (though it is amusing if you can smack someone/
thing in the face with it). Actually, meat balls/chunks are the worst,
in terms of traditional food. Corpses are worse than any other food,
and don't last very long.

As for the invisible mind flayer, man, that's rough! Any time I get a
flayer flittering through my mind I either keep my towel on or at
least keep track of the beast by putting it on and off consistently
until I've done away with the menace. Amnesia makes me almost quit
when I get nailed by it. I almost never think to use a sustain ability
ring... does the ring just protection your INT score, or does it also
prevent the amnesia aspect of the flayers' attack? I'd imagine not,
but I'd love to know that.

Lacking any access to holy water for a long time can be a real trial.
It can also be a big cause for massive (again, often tedious)
stashing. Not to mention preventing you from using some possibly great
items!


